From: Fabien Danieau <fabien.danieau@pollen-robotics.com>
Subject: [PATCH] scripts/resource_tool: zero index entries before writing them

pack_image() fills one index_tbl_entry on the stack per resource and writes
it out whole. The entry is never cleared, and hash[] is 32 bytes while the
SHA-1 copied into it is 20, so bytes 20..31 of every hash field are whatever
was on the stack -- part of a 0x00007ffc... userspace address, which ASLR
changes on every run. resource.img, and the boot.img that embeds it, therefore
differ between two builds of identical inputs.

Zero the entry once before the loop. Every field the loop sets is still set;
the unused tail of hash[] is now 0.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
--- a/scripts/resource_tool.c
+++ b/scripts/resource_tool.c
@@ -1480,6 +1480,7 @@
 	index_tbl_entry entry;
 	char hash[20];	/* sha1 */
 	int i;
+	memset(&entry, 0, sizeof(entry));

 	memcpy(entry.tag, INDEX_TBL_ENTR_TAG, sizeof(entry.tag));
 	for (i = 0; i < file_num; i++) {
